<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zoskales</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zoskales was a king associated with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aksumite-empire">Aksum</a> in the first century CE, the earliest Aksumite ruler named in a written source. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/periplus-of-the-erythraean-sea">Periplus of the Erythraean Sea</a> describes him as Greek-educated. This is the first evidence of Aksum's cosmopolitan engagement with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greco-roman-world">Greco-Roman world</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zoskales.jpg" alt="Zoskales" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zheim · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ethio_w3.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
